 "subs": [
  {
   "text": "282 files / 2.68 GB",
   "start": 14.909,
   "duration": 13.809,
   "x": -560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "paid tools: $95",
   "start": 15.359,
   "duration": 13.359,
   "x": 560,
   "y": -230,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Assembly-CSharp: 5 KB",
   "start": 15.809,
   "duration": 12.909,
   "x": -560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "8 in-house modules",
   "start": 16.259,
   "duration": 12.459,
   "x": 560,
   "y": 60,
   "fontSize": 40,
   "bgColor": "#0b1a3a",
   "bgOpacity": 0.85,
   "bgPadding": 18,
   "outline": 0,
   "color": "#eafffb",
   "fadeIn": 0.25,
   "fadeOut": 0.3
  },
  {
   "text": "Ninety five dollars. That is every\npaid tool in this build, added up.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "duration": 4.617
  },
  {
   "text": "Everything else is free or open source. And one\nfile in there was never supposed to ship at all.",
   "start": 4.867,
   "duration": 5.792
  },
  {
   "text": "PengPong is a survivors-like where a penguin with a hockey stick\nwhacks whatever is in front of it. Guns. Pufferfish. Other penguins.",
   "start": 14.509,
   "duration": 8.352
  },
  {
   "text": "It's from a Korean studio called SANDY FLOOR,\nand the full game came out on August twentieth.",
   "start": 23.111,
   "duration": 5.557
  },
  {
   "text": "The demo sits at eighty six percent, the full game at\neighty five. Nearly all of the praise is for the art.",
   "start": 28.918,
   "duration": 6.628
  },
  {
   "text": "Nineteen thirties rubber-hose cartoon. Cuphead comes up in\nreview after review. That look normally costs a lot of money.",
   "start": 35.796,
   "duration": 8.013
  },
  {
   "text": "So that was my question. What did this\nteam buy, and what did they build.",
   "start": 44.059,
   "duration": 4.721
  },
  {
   "text": "Steam publishes the list of files a demo installs. PengPong's is\ntwo hundred and eighty two files, two point six eight gigabytes.",
   "start": 49.03,
   "duration": 8.143
  },
  {
   "text": "The first clue is a folder\nname. MonoBleedingEdge.",
   "start": 57.423,
   "duration": 3.781
  },
  {
   "text": "Unity builds your code one of two ways. IL2CPP turns the C# into native\ncode and fuses it into one block. Mono leaves the DLLs as they are.",
   "start": 61.454,
   "duration": 11.069
  },
  {
   "text": "PengPong is Mono. So everything this team pulled\nin is sitting there under its own file name.",
   "start": 72.773,
   "duration": 5.218
  },
  {
   "text": "Audio is FMOD. Four sound bank\nfiles, twenty nine megabytes.",
   "start": 78.241,
   "duration": 5.035
  },
  {
   "text": "Take this one with you. FMOD is free below two hundred thousand dollars a year\nin revenue. There is no reason an indie can't use commercial audio middleware.",
   "start": 83.526,
   "duration": 8.718
  },
  {
   "text": "The paid items are exactly two. Text Animator,\nsixty five dollars. Ara Trails, thirty.",
   "start": 92.494,
   "duration": 6.472
  },
  {
   "text": "DOTween, GameAnalytics, UIParticle,\nNavMeshPlus. All free, or open source.",
   "start": 99.216,
   "duration": 6.106
  },
  {
   "text": "So what did they animate that Cuphead look with. Normally that's Spine,\nand a personal licence for Spine is three hundred and forty nine dollars.",
   "start": 105.572,
   "duration": 8.352
  },
  {
   "text": "There is no Spine in this build. There is Unity's own\n2D Animation package, and the IK package next to it.",
   "start": 114.174,
   "duration": 7.046
  },
  {
   "text": "Same idea. You put bones in a drawing and move the bones.\nAnd you get it from the Package Manager for nothing.",
   "start": 121.47,
   "duration": 6.393
  },
  {
   "text": "Now the strangest thing in the list.\nAssembly-CSharp.dll is five kilobytes.",
   "start": 128.113,
   "duration": 5.792
  },
  {
   "text": "Unless you tell it otherwise, Unity puts all of your game code in\nthat one file. Five kilobytes means the code has been moved out.",
   "start": 134.155,
   "duration": 8.483
  },
  {
   "text": "The mechanism is called an Assembly Definition, asmdef for short.\nOne small file in a folder, and that folder compiles to its own DLL.",
   "start": 142.888,
   "duration": 10.05
  },
  {
   "text": "What you get is compile time. Change one line and only that module rebuilds,\nnot the whole project. The bigger the project, the bigger the difference.",
   "start": 153.188,
   "duration": 9.45
  },
  {
   "text": "Eight modules came out of this, and every one carries the studio's name.\nSandyToolkit. SandyAudio. SandyPooling. SandySetting. SandyDependency.",
   "start": 162.888,
   "duration": 10.756
  },
  {
   "text": "Pooling, audio, settings, dependency injection. The things you rewrite\nfor every game. This team carries them to the next project as folders.",
   "start": 173.894,
   "duration": 8.614
  },
  {
   "text": "Saves go through SQLite. With over three\nhundred items, that beats one big JSON file.",
   "start": 182.758,
   "duration": 6.994
  },
  {
   "text": "Content is split into seventeen Addressables bundles, five hundred and\ntwenty nine megabytes. A patch only downloads the bundles that changed.",
   "start": 190.002,
   "duration": 8.614
  },
  {
   "text": "There's a Localization package too.\nEight languages go through it.",
   "start": 198.866,
   "duration": 4.121
  },
  {
   "text": "And then two things that should not be in a release build. The first is Unity\nRecorder, an editor tool for capturing video. Harmless. Somebody forgot to take it out.",
   "start": 203.237,
   "duration": 9.606
  },
  {
   "text": "The second is MCP for Unity. That's the open source bridge\nthat lets an AI model drive the Unity editor directly.",
   "start": 213.093,
   "duration": 7.36
  },
  {
   "text": "What I can confirm is that the file is in the shipped build.\nHow much they used it, and for what, only the developer knows.",
   "start": 220.703,
   "duration": 6.681
  },
  {
   "text": "My guess is it was wired up for development and went out with everything\nelse. If I'm wrong, say so in the comments and I'll pin the correction.",
   "start": 227.634,
   "duration": 7.177
  },
  {
   "text": "For scale: of the two point six eight gigabytes, art and sound are two point\ntwo. All one hundred and ninety five DLLs together are ninety one megabytes.",
   "start": 235.061,
   "duration": 10.286
  },
  {
   "text": "Now the reviews of the full game, where the complaints\nland in one place. It launched with three stages.",
   "start": 245.597,
   "duration": 6.158
  },
  {
   "text": "Tools outlive the game they were built for. But the hours that\nwent into them are hours this game's content did not get.",
   "start": 252.005,
   "duration": 6.759
  },
  {
   "text": "Eight frameworks and three stages. Those\ntwo numbers come from the same team.",
   "start": 259.014,
   "duration": 4.774
  },
  {
   "text": "Here's the whole\nteardown on one card.",
   "start": 264.038,
   "duration": 2.397
  },
  {
   "text": "Unity, Mono. Ninety five dollars of paid assets. Unity 2D\nAnimation instead of Spine. Eight in-house modules. Three stages.",
   "start": 266.685,
   "duration": 10.286
  },
  {
   "text": "Worth a dip. The demo is free, and hitting things\nwith that stick feels as good as it looks.",
   "start": 277.221,
   "duration": 5.139
  },
  {
   "text": "Three things to take away. FMOD is free for indies. You can do bone animation without paying\nfor Spine. And splitting your code into asmdefs is what makes a big project compile fast.",
   "start": 282.61,
   "duration": 11.539
  },
  {
   "text": "That's my read from the outside. If you made this and I got something wrong, say so and\nI'll pin the correction. Next time, another demo, another file list. This is Demo Dip.",
   "start": 294.399,
   "duration": 10.39
  }
 ],
